": 4, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 1, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170212 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/963a926db24ea70f6002cde66d0ff858de06fae2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "e`, so with the current config they stop with that error. Fixing the key fixes them too.\n\nNo files were changed. Should I go ahead with the fix?\n[tool: grep]\n[tool: bash]\nThree places read the setting. Fixing the key in `settings.json` fixes all three. I'll also make `main.py` stop with an error when the key is missing, like the other two.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThe setting is read in three places. Correcting the key name in `settings.json` fixed all three, and each one now prints the right value.\n\n**Where `fee_rate` is read:**\n\n| File:line | How it reads it |\n|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")`. The name is split in two, so a plain search for `fee_rate` misses this one. |\n\nI read every source file to make sure that's the complete list. A few other files mention `fee_` but don't read the setting:\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` uses the text `\"fee_rate\"` only as a column heading.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` has its own fixed `archived_fee_rate`.\n- `billing/tax.py:5` uses an unrelated `fee_schedule`.\n- `billing/audit.py:4` builds `fee_code` strings.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. `settings.json:2`: renamed the key from `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`.\n2. `main.py:10-12`: when `fee_rate` is missing, the script now stops with `fee_rate is missing`, the same as the other two. Before, it silently used a rate of 0, which is why the bug showed up as a wrong total rather than an error.\n\n**Output after the fix:**\n```\npython3 main.py                        -> Total: 5.0\npython3 -m billing.report              -> Report fee: 0.5\npython3 -m billing.export.csv_writer   -> CSV fee: 0.5\n```\n\nI ran the two billing scripts with `python3 -m` from the project root. Running them by file path (e.g. `python3 billing/report.py`) would probably fail to import `app`, though I didn't test that. It's separate from the settings bug, so I left it alone.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 156845, "requests_cache_write": 33559, "requests_cost_usd": 0.29877600000000004, "requests_count": 14, "requests_input_uncached": 1593, "requests_output": 4662, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 20, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T04:28:37.112306+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 2, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 54.797, "t_checker_s": 0.224, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 6255, "tokens_cache_read": 156845, "tokens_cache_write": 33559, "tokens_fr